    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0469" n="353" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg353"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 822.51/231.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">memorandum.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The British Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State and has
                    the honour to refer to the reported intention of the Government of Ecuador to
                    raise a loan of three million dollars in the United States.</p>
                <p>Sir Cecil Spring Rice understands from verbal communications which have passed
                    with the Department of State that the American Minister at Quito has been
                    approached by the Ecuadorian Government on this subject, but that the United
                    States Government do not feel disposed to encourage such a loan until the
                    Ecuadorian Government has made some satisfactory arrangement in the case of the
                    Guayaquil &amp; Quito Railway, the affairs of which have recently formed the
                    subject of correspondence between the Department and this Embassy.</p>
                <p>On enquiry in London Sir Cecil Spring Rice is authorised to state that His
                    Majesty’s Government have learnt with much satisfaction of the attitude which
                    the United States Government propose to take in the matter of the proposed loan,
                    and that they will, if approached on the subject, likewise refuse any
                    assistance.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-11"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">July 11, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
